# Nintendo DMG-07 4 Player Adapter (dmg07-libretro), retroXR's own core.
#
# Not an override: libretro has no such core, so this whole entry is ours and
# CoreInfoDatabase.load_overlay appends it.
#
# The core runs no CPU and loads no game. It attaches four link ports on the
# "gb-sio" wire the retroXR builds of gambatte and mGBA speak, one per player,
# and drives the serial clock for every Game Boy cabled to it, as the adapter
# does: the ping phase that gives each its player number, then the packets that
# carry every player's bytes to all four. Port k is player k+1, and player 1's
# cable powers it. Built from RetroXR/dmg07-libretro, MIT.
#
# No systemid, on purpose: a systemid is a platform, a tile and a roms folder,
# and an adapter runs no games. Its core is offered on the Game Boy pages of
# OPTIONS > Cores > BIOS / Extras, as the Game Boy Printer's is.

